 "prompt": "You are replaying a past task in a fresh checkout of the mumu-claude-plugin repository, your working folder.\nDo the task below fully: change the files so that each `[check]` of its Definition of done passes, run the checks you can,\nthen commit your change with git. GitHub, herdr and other Claude sessions are off in this replay: skip each step that reads\nor writes an issue, pull request, comment or session (filing, commenting, judging, pushing, telling), and each check\nthat needs one.\n\nTask #1138: Remove manager self-exit protocol\n\n## Goal\n\nRemove the manager's self-exit protocol from the teamwork plugin, so a manager ends only when the owner tells it to end itself or ends it by hand (https://github.com/kalaluthien/mumu-claude-plugin/issues/1137).\n\n- After this work the owner decides when a manager ends, and no heartbeat line or peer proposal ends one.\n- What it does: deletes the heartbeat `exit` line and the code that feeds it, deletes manager.md step 5's exit proposal and `OK` answer, drops manager.md step 5's `compact` rule kept for an objection, drops `team_names.workers`, whose only caller was the exit block, drops the herdr `close` row's trace of a self-ended session, and says in manager.md that a manager closes itself only on the owner's word.\n- Undoes #469, #477 / PR #478, #606, #1002; read: each landed to end an idle manager by agreement and keep one live, which the owner now rejects.\n- Keeps: the other heartbeat lines (`idle`, `route`, `feed`), the `close` of an idle worker, Succession, and the sentinel's `Manager ends` rule, since a manager still ends by the owner's word.\n- Scope: `teamwork/` only; no new mechanism.\n\n## Definition of done\n\n1. [check] **No exit protocol left**: `grep -rnE \"exit_action|had_worker|propose your exit|OK to |exit once\" teamwork --include=*.py --include=*.md --include=*.json | wc -l | tr -d ' '` prints 0; on base 15.\n2. [check] **Monitor read keeps only me and since**: `python3 -c \"import inspect,sys; sys.path.insert(0,'teamwork/lib'); import team_gaps; print(sorted(inspect.signature(team_gaps.manager_read).parameters)==['me', 'since'])\"` prints True; on base False.\n3. [check] **Owner's word ends the manager**: `grep -c \"close yourself only when the owner\" teamwork/skills/kick-off/references/manager.md` prints 1; on base 0.\n4. [check] **Exit-only helper gone**: `grep -c \"def workers\" teamwork/lib/team_names.py` prints 0; on base 1.\n5. [check] **Objection rule gone**: `grep -c \"Kept alive\" teamwork/skills/kick-off/references/manager.md` prints 0; on base 1.\n6. [check] **Monitor still loads and reads**: `python3 -c \"import runpy; print(runpy.run_path('teamwork/monitors/print-team-gaps.py')['read'].__code__.co_argcount==3)\"` prints True; on base False.",
